      <div class="kicker">About the project</div>
      <h1>Most music writing talks to the famous. This talks to everyone else.</h1>
      <p>The Session Notes is a series of interviews with the people who make music work: the players, teachers, engineers, bookers, managers, and label people doing the daily work of a music career. Every two weeks, one new conversation.</p>
      <p>Every interview ends with the same question: <em>who should I talk to next?</em> That is how this grows, one introduction at a time, from local musicians toward the wider industry.</p>

      <div class="bio-divider"></div>

      <div class="kicker">About the writer</div>
      <p>The Session Notes is written by Damon Uyehara, a senior at Fremont High School in Sunnyvale, California.</p>
      <p>Damon came up through high school band and drumline. In 2026 he performed as a snare drummer with Blue Devils C in stadiums including the Rose Bowl and Stanford Stadium. That experience sparked a deeper curiosity about how working musicians and artists actually grow, what their creative process looks like, and how the business really works.</p>
      <p>This project is his attempt to find out by talking to the people already inside the industry. Damon plans to build a career in music, supporting artists and contributing to the growth of the scene, and these conversations are where that work begins.</p>

